---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<Section
  id="agents"
  title="Your agent gets a lane of its own, and the daemon keeps it running."
  more={{ href: '/agents/', label: 'More about agents' }}
>
  <p>
    An agent starts a stack for its branch with the same commands you use, hands you a localhost
    URL, and moves on. Its shell can end; the daemon owns the processes. A second agent on the same
    machine gets lane 4, not a port conflict.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Claude Code and Codex plugin teaches the agent the CLI and refuses a dev server started in
    the background, where nothing supervises it and its logs are lost.
  </p>
  <Terminal slot="visual" title="agent session">
    <div class="chat">
      <p class="chat-you">start the stack and give me the URL</p>
      <div class="chat-agent">
        <pre><span class="command">devlanes start</span>
myapp@3 (agent/perf): 3/3 ready
<span class="success">ready</span> api    http://127.0.0.1:20030  <span class="url">https://api.myapp3.localhost</span>
<span class="success">ready</span> web    http://127.0.0.1:20031  <span class="url">https://myapp3.localhost</span>
<span class="success">ready</span> worker http://127.0.0.1:20032</pre>
        <p>
          Up on lane 3, main is untouched on lane 0:{' '}
          <span class="url">https://myapp3.localhost</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Terminal>
</Section>
